      {
        "id": "comment",
        "type": "nodetool.workflows.base_node.Comment",
        "data": {
          "comment": "# 🔎 Research a Brand from Its Website\n\nPaste a website. An agent opens it, searches for what the site leaves out, and writes research notes with sources. An extractor then turns the notes into the five fields a brand kit needs: name, audience, voice, one-line description and tagline.\n\n**Agentic step:** the agent decides which pages to open and what to search for. It reports what it could not confirm instead of inventing it.\n\n**Try this:** point it at your own site, then edit any field before you generate assets from it."
        },
        "ui_properties": {
          "position": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 0
          },
          "zIndex": 0,
          "width": 560,
          "selectable": true,
          "bypassed": false,
          "height": 266
        },
        "dynamic_properties": {},
        "dynamic_outputs": {}
      },
      {
        "id": "in_website",
        "type": "nodetool.input.StringInput",
        "data": {
          "name": "website",
          "value": "https://nodetool.ai",
          "description": "The brand's website. The agent starts here."
        },
        "ui_properties": {
          "position": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 877
          },
          "zIndex": 0,
          "width": 300,
          "title": "1️⃣ Website",
          "selectable": true,
          "bypassed": false
        },
        "dynamic_properties": {},
        "dynamic_outputs": {}
      },
      {
        "id": "research_prompt",
        "type": "nodetool.text.Prompt",
        "data": {
          "prompt": "Research the brand behind this website: {{ WEBSITE }}\n\n1. Open the website with the browser tool. Open one or two more pages from it if the home page is thin, such as About or Pricing.\n2. Use web search once or twice for what the site does not say: who uses the product and how others describe the brand.\n3. Write research notes in Markdown with these sections:\n\n## Brand\nThe brand name exactly as the site writes it, and what it sells, in one or two sentences.\n\n## Audience\nWho it is for, as specifically as the evidence allows.\n\n## Voice\nThree adjectives for the tone of the site's copy, each with a short quote from the site that shows it.\n\n## Tagline\nThe site's own tagline or headline if it has one. Otherwise propose one of at most six words and say it is proposed.\n\n## Colors\nThe main brand colors you saw, as hex codes if the page exposes them.\n\n## Sources\nEvery URL you used.\n\nUse at most eight tool calls in total, then write the notes. If a page refuses to load, say so and move on. Write \"Not confirmed\" for anything you could not find. Do not invent facts."
        },
        "ui_properties": {
          "position": {
            "x": 400,
            "y": 761
          },
          "zIndex": 0,
          "width": 320,
          "title": "Research brief",
          "selectable": true,
          "bypassed": false,
          "height": 360
        },
        "dynamic_properties": {
          "WEBSITE": ""
        },
        "dynamic_outputs": {}
      },
